n is only an imperfect copy that agrees with probability r, cooperating and defecting have different expected values, and cooperation wins only when r is above about 0.5005.\n\nI'm checking the twin case with a noisy copy: the twin matches my choice with probability r, so defecting pays 1,001,000 when the twin cooperates and 1,000 when it defects, and that's the expected value I'm comparing against cooperation.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":83920,"completion_tokens":13361,"total_tokens":97281,"cost":0.30145,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.30145,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.16784,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.13361},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":5269,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}